  "info": "the snowy tree cricket chirps faster when it's warmer — so the BPM literally is the temperature (Dolbear's Law, roughly 40 plus chirps-per-15-seconds) — a warm-night downtempo where a kalimba answers the field, and the tempo tells you to open a window",
